❯ Write exactly one paragraph of about 90 words about
  lighthouses. Use no line breaks, no markdown, no lists.
  This instruction sentence is padded so the prompt itself
  is long enough to wrap: alpha bravo charlie delta echo
  foxtrot golf hotel india juliet kilo lima mike.

⏺ Lighthouses have guided sailors for thousands of years.
  Early towers used open fires to warn ships away from
  dangerous rocks. Later, engineers built taller stone
  towers with powerful lamps and large glass lenses that
  threw light far across the water. Today, most lighthouses
  run on electricity, and some use automated systems instead
  of keepers. Many have become museums or tourist sites,
  but they still mark coastlines and help ships find safe
  passage through fog, storms, and darkness. Their steady
  beams remind us how much careful design and human courage
  can protect lives at sea.

